    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0585" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v23/pg538"/>

                <head>227. Backchannel Message From the White House Situation Room to the Embassy in
                        Panama<anchor n="1" xml:id="d227-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-05-17T19:09:00+00:00">May 17, 1978, 1909Z</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>WH80697. Panama: Please deliver to Mr. Bob
                        Pastor, National Security Council, with the Staff Advance
                    Team.</p>
                <p>(State 125048.) Subject: GOC Reaction to
                    Situation in Dominican Rep. Ref: Bogota 4658; Barnebey-Drexler telcons May 17.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d227-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>1. Confirming telcons, Department is most appreciative for GOC offer to make demarche and take other
                    diplomatic steps to help safeguard Dominican democracy. We have made efforts
                    along these lines, including the Secretary’s having sent a personal letter to
                        Balaguer.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d227-f3"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0586" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/>
                <p>2. Situation in Santo Domingo has improved. Military commanders have agreed to
                    recognize results of elections. City is calm.</p>
                <p>3. In effort to undergird GODR resolve to
                    maintain democratic system, we believe it would be helpful for Colombians to
                    make demarche in Santo Domingo. We also understand Venezuelans are making a
                    similar approach.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d227-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    Vance
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d227-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d227-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 8, Folder: Backchannel Messages: Latin America: 6/77–12/78.
                    Confidential; Sensitive; Immediate.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d227-f2" n="2" xml:id="d227-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 4658 from Bogota, May 17, the Embassy wrote about a Colombian offer
                    to assist the United States in regard to the elections in the Dominican
                    Republic. (National Archives, RG 59, Central
                    Foreign Policy File, D780208–0027) No record of the telephone conversations has
                    been found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d227-f3" n="3" xml:id="d227-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d226">Document 226</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d227-f4" n="4" xml:id="d227-f4-content">
                <p>Backchannel message WH80705, May 17, informed Pastor that Venezuela, Costa Rica, Panama, and Colombia
                    delivered démarches “urging the results of the [Dominican] vote be honored.”
                    (Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject File,
                    Box 8, Folder: Backchannel Messages: Latin America: 6/77–12/78)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
